Description: Silent by default. Loud when it matters. Lightweight defensive security daemon
 for Linux.
 Hermian detects high-confidence signs of compromise on a Linux host using
 deterministic, contextual detection (process chains, SSH abuse, persistence,
 privilege escalation, anomalous network behavior) and alerts locally or via
 Telegram, email or webhook. No dashboard, no YAML rules, no alert fatigue:
 install, enable, forget - Hermian only interrupts you when it matters.

